e": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "South Dakota remains one of the most reliably Republican states in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of roughly fifteen points toward the GOP and no Democratic presidential win since 1964. The 2028 race features an open field, since the incumbent president is term-limited, which removes any incumbency advantage from either side.\n\nNo public polls of the state or expert ratings are available yet, so the forecast rests on the state's underlying partisan alignment. National coverage of the 2028 primaries shows competitive fields on both sides, but nothing so far indicates a change in South Dakota's basic orientation. The state is expected to back the Republican nominee by a comfortable margin, though the long horizon and lack of state-level data leave room for movement if the national environment shifts sharply.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0482, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0894, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0882, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0844, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0865, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0843, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0921, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.078, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0834, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0867, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0898, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0794, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-